What upstream lacks (hermes-agent v0.23.0, apps/desktop/src/store/connections.ts):
a first sign-in when the user picks an OAuth gateway that has no session yet.

selectConnection() dials the target and proves it with GET /api/profiles.
Without a session that read gets a 401, and the main process answers it
with its *silent* re-login (fetchJsonViaOauthSession -> retryCookie401WithLogin
-> openOauthLoginWindow({ silent: true, background: true })): a hidden
window that loads /, follows the redirect to the identity provider and
gives up after 12 s. An IdP that needs the user (pocket-id with
prompt=login, a passkey) is never shown, so the pick ends in the toast
"Could not connect to <label>: ... not signed in. Open Settings ->
Gateway and click Sign in". Only Settings' Sign in button runs the
interactive login (system browser for gateways advertising native_pkce,
a visible window otherwise), so every newly added OAuth remote, e.g. one
seeded into connections.json by the Nix launcher, stays unreachable from
the sidebar until the user finds that button.

This hunk: when a user pick (not a boot restore) of an OAuth remote/cloud
entry fails with a sign-in error (isRemoteReauthError, the boot overlay's
test), run that same interactive login for the entry's url and
connection id (the id keeps the session in the entry's own cookie jar),
then dial once more. A cancelled or failed login rethrows the original
error, as before.

